
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <%- include("./partials/head.ejs") %>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles/texty.css" />
</head>
<body>
    <header>
        <%- include("./partials/navbar.ejs") %>
    </header>
    <main>
        <section>
            <h1>Rambling a bit.</h1>Its a bit long so bear with me :)
            <p>
                Spar is a Ghanaian card game so it might not be so popular to people outside Ghana.
                Give it a try though it's very interesting, and fun of course. There are many variations
                of it so I implemented the one which is common in my region. It doesn't use a full 52 card deck.
                5 cards down to aces of each suit are removed from the deck to leave 32 cards to play with.
            </p>
        </section>
        <section>
            <h1>Pregame</h1>
            <p>
                5 cards are dealt to each player from the deck. A hand can be valid or invalid. Invalidity of a hand
                awards a player a removal of two usually random cards with a replacement of two new ones from the deck.
                The types of invalid hands are as follows:
                <ul>
                    <li>No Pic No Ten: Your hand has neither a picture card (Jack, Queen or King) nor a 10 in it</li>
                    <li>Hands: All cards in your hand are of the same suit</li>
                    <li>Triple six: You have 3 or more sixes in your hand. The random removal is only done from the sixes in this case.</li>
                </ul>
                When all cards have been used once and there are no cards left to pick from. The deck is shuffled.
                An invalid hand can still be played with hence you can choose whether you want cards removed or not.
                After the hand is to your liking, press Ready to start the round.
            </p>
        </section>
        <section>
            <h1>Game Objective</h1>
            <p>
                The aim of the game is to gain the most points by leading the last trick of each round.
            </p>
        </section>
        <section>
            <h1>On my Turn?</h1>
            <p>
                The game is played in five tricks. On your turn, you play any of the cards you have in your hand onto the board.
                Your opponent must respond with a card of the same suit if they have one, or a card of any suit if they don't.
                If they do not have one of the same suit, you lead the trick.
                If they do, the leader of the trick is the player with the higher card. After each trick, the leader goes on to
                deal a card in the next trick with a response following until all cards in a hand have been dealt.
            </p>
        </section>
        <section>
            <h1>When does it end?</h1>
            <p>
                The round ends when all cards in both hands have been dealt. The leader of the last trick wins the round.
                Points are added to the winners score based on his last card. 7-faced cards count for 2 points and 6-faced
                cards count for 3 points. All other (larger) cards count for one point. When the last few cards comprise
                stacked 6s and 7s, the total score is the sum of each of the cards in the stack. For example, if the winning
                hand is a King of Diamond, Queen of Diamond, 6 of Hearts, 7 of Clubs, and 6 of Diamonds, the 6H contributes 3
                points, the 7C contributes 2 points and the 6D contributes 3 points making a total of 8 points. Stacking ends
                when a larger card is met or when a suit repeats more than once. So if in our example, 
                instead of the 6 of Hearts, it was the 6 of Clubs, the stacking would end at the 7C to make just 5 points.
                Hopefully that makes sense :)
            </p>
        </section>
        <section>
            <h1>Anything Else?</h1>
            <p>
                After points have been assigned, you can make two claims:
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        No be game: This means that an unplayable game occured. This is usually when a player does not have
                        any suit in common with their opponent, like an all-spades hand vs and all-diamonds hand, or an all-red
                        hand vs an all-black hand. Hands situation also counts as an unplayable hand. In both cases. The game is scrapped.
                        All points gained by this round are withdrawn and the game is restarted with new hands.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        Gba: This is a rule that means that there was a violation of the game somewhere else. It is accepted if
                        a player refuses to respond with a card of the same suit even though he has one in his hand. Gba is called,
                        3 points are deducted from the player committing the offense. All point gains are withdrawn and the game
                        is restarted with new hands. Don't mindlessly call this one though, because if you're wrong, you get a deduction
                        of one point.
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </p>
            <p>
                Anyone can move on to the next game, but there is a five second wait before that can be done. It is within this time
                limit that you can make these calls, if you do not call, an opponent is able to move on to the next round, banking the unfair
                points for themselves, so be on your toes.
            </p>
        </section>
    </main>
    <script>
            // definition of variables
            const showNavbarActions = document.getElementById("navbarDropdownButton");
            const navbarLine = document.getElementById("navbarLine");
            const navbarActions = document.getElementById("navbarActions");
            const mediaQuery = window.matchMedia("(max-width: 760px)");
            
            let isNavbarToggled = false;

            // toggle navbar dropdown on or off
            showNavbarActions.addEventListener("click", () => {
                isNavbarToggled = !isNavbarToggled;
                if (isNavbarToggled) {
                    navbarLine.className = "navbar-line";
                    navbarActions.className = "navbar-actions"
                    showNavbarActions.innerHTML = "&#x25B2;";
                } else {
                    navbarLine.className = "navbar-line hidden";
                    navbarActions.className = "navbar-actions hidden";
                    showNavbarActions.innerHTML = "&#x25BC;";
                }
            });
            function handleMediaChange(e) {
                navbarLine.className = "navbar-line hidden";
                isNavbarToggled = false;
                if (e.matches) {
                    showNavbarActions.innerHTML = "&#x25BC;";
                    navbarActions.className = "navbar-actions hidden"
                    showNavbarActions.className = "";
                } else {
                    showNavbarActions.className = "hidden";
                    navbarActions.className = "navbar-actions"
                }
            }
            mediaQuery.addEventListener("change", e => handleMediaChange(e))
            handleMediaChange(mediaQuery);
    </script>
</body>

</html>
